  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN stones numbered 111 through NNN. Each stone has a value written on it; for each valid iii, the value on stone iii is ViV_iVi​.\n\nYou are initially on the first stone and your goal is to jump to stone NNN by perfoming a valid sequence of jumps. Formally, let's denote a sequence of visited stones during these jumps by S1,S2,…,SMS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_MS1​,S2​,…,SM​, where M−1M-1M−1 is the number of jumps. Then, the following conditions must be satisfied:\n\n\n1=S1&lt;S2&lt;…&lt;SM=N1 = S_1 \\lt S_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt S_M = N1=S1​&lt;S2​&lt;…&lt;SM​=N\nfor each iii (1≤i&lt;M1 \\le i \\lt M1≤i&lt;M), min⁡(VS1,VS2,…,VSi)+max⁡(VSi+1,…,VSM)=Si+1−Si\\min(V_{S_1}, V_{S_2}, \\ldots, V_{S_i}) + \\max(V_{S_{i+1}}, \\ldots, V_{S_M}) = S_{i+1} - S_imin(VS1​​,VS2​​,…,VSi​​)+max(VSi+1​​,…,VSM​​)=Si+1​−Si​, which is the length of the iii-th jump\nFind the minimum number of jumps needed to reach stone NNN, or report that it is impossible to reach stone NNN using valid jumps.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers V1,V2,…,VNV_1, V_2, \\ldots, V_NV1​,V2​,…,VN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer --- the minimum number of jumps, or −1-1−1 if it is impossible to reach stone NNN.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\leq T \\leq 501≤T≤50",
      "2≤N≤5002 \\leq N \\leq 5002≤N≤500",
      "1≤Vi≤N1 \\leq V_i \\leq N1≤Vi​≤N for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500500500",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (15 points):** Vi≤2V_i \\le 2Vi​≤2 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #2 (35 points):** the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 100100100",
      "**Subtask #3 (50 points):** original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 1\n5\n1 3 4 1 2\n11\n1 4 5 3 2 8 3 4 3 7 1",
        "output": "1\n-1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: You can jump from stone 111 to stone NNN directly because min⁡(V1)+max⁡(VN)=2\\min(V_1) + \\max(V_N) = 2min(V1​)+max(VN​)=2 and the length of the jump is exactly 222.\nExample case 2: It is impossible to reach stone NNN.\nExample case 3: One valid sequence of visited stones which uses the minimum number or jumps is (1,5,9,11)(1, 5, 9, 11)(1,5,9,11). It is valid because the lengths of the jumps are:\n\nfirst jump: min⁡(V1)+max⁡(V5,V9,V11)=4\\min(V_1) + \\max(V_5, V_9, V_{11}) = 4min(V1​)+max(V5​,V9​,V11​)=4\nsecond jump: min⁡(V1,V5)+max⁡(V9,V11)=4\\min(V_1, V_5) + \\max(V_9, V_{11}) = 4min(V1​,V5​)+max(V9​,V11​)=4\nthird jump: min⁡(V1,V5,V9)+max⁡(V11)=2\\min(V_1, V_5, V_9) + \\max(V_{11}) = 2min(V1​,V5​,V9​)+max(V11​)=2"
      }
    ]
